__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
.venv/

# **No artwork, and no measured corpora.** The reference library is built from private collections of illustrations; the
# distribution it produces is shared as tests/data/corpus_summary.json, and the images and the raw per-image records are
# not. Ignored here so that a corpus placed beside the code by habit cannot be committed by accident -- a rule that
# depends on remembering is not a rule.
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.webp
*.bmp
*.tif
*.tiff
*.gif
*.psd
*.fla
*.xfl
*.ai
*.svg
*.jsonl

# **But the hand-written error table is a document, not a corpus.** learn/errors.jsonl is the table of patterns the
# pipeline got wrong, written by hand after looking at a drawing. The rule above exists to keep measured per-image
# records out, and a path exception is still a rule rather than a thing to remember. Without this line the table three
# work is untracked, and a clone would not contain the part that took the longest to find.
!learn/errors.jsonl
